// credentials as the HTTP API. It first checks for a JWT in the ?token= query
// parameter, then the configured auth cookie (including opaque sid sessions),
// and finally falls back to the JSON auth frame protocol. Supporting the cookie
// here is important for browser clients because WebSocket handshakes include
// cookies, while JavaScript cannot attach an Authorization header.
